infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Ack ordering: pick which failure you accept
  desc A crash in the work-to-ack window fails either way — you choose loss or duplication
  compares
    - label Ack BEFORE processing
      children
        - label Order: acknowledge, then do the work
          desc Commit the offset or ack first, charge second
        - label Effect: at-most-once
          desc No redelivery once acknowledged
        - label Crash in the window LOSES it
          desc The charge never happens and is never retried
        - label Rejected for payments
          desc Trades a double-charge for a silent missed charge
    - label Ack AFTER processing
      children
        - label Order: do the work, then acknowledge
          desc Charge first, commit the offset or ack second
        - label Effect: at-least-once
          desc The default for Kafka, NATS JetStream, RabbitMQ
        - label Crash in the window DUPLICATES it
          desc Broker redelivers and the card is charged twice
        - label The senior pick
          desc Pair with idempotency to get effectively-once
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
